:: R4_Choice_A [r4 story]
<<location "Victoria Cross's Office, Floor 42">>
<<objective "Leave Victoria's office.">>

I should leave. She said I could go. The pen is moving on the paper. I'm already dismissed.

But.

<<sayself>>Ms. Cross.<</sayself>>

The pen stops.

<<sayself>>What comes next?<</sayself>>

She looks up. Studies me. The question is a tell. She knows it and now I know she knows it. Asking what comes next means I'm not running. It means the door she opened, I'm looking through it instead of slamming it shut. It means eagerness dressed up as practicality.

Her smile widens. A fraction. The kind of widening that on another face might be called warmth.

<<say "Victoria Cross">>Patience, Daniel. That's what comes next.<</say>>

She looks back down. The pen resumes. I leave. But the word patience hangs in the elevator like perfume. It implies a timeline. A plan. A sequence of events she's already plotted on a calendar I'll never see.

Patience means there is more and I asked for it.

