:: R4_Choice_B [r4 story]
<<location "Victoria Cross's Office, Floor 42">>
<<objective "Leave Victoria's office.">>

<<sayself>>What's the endgame here?<</sayself>>

The words come out sharper than I intend. Or maybe exactly as sharp as I intend. Self-defense dressed up as a question. The last gasp of a man who just admitted that wearing women's underwear felt good and needs to reassert control over something, anything.

Victoria's expression cools. Not cold. Cooler. The temperature change of a room when someone opens a window a crack.

<<say "Victoria Cross">>You don't get to ask that yet.<</say>>

<<sayself>>Yet implies I will eventually.<</sayself>>

<<say "Victoria Cross">>It implies I decide when. Which is the point of all of this, Daniel. I decide. You said yes. The "when" and "what" are mine now.<</say>>

She holds my gaze. I hold hers. Two people in a locked office on the forty-second floor, having a conversation about power while the city darkens outside. She wins. She was always going to win. She was winning before I knocked on the door.

I leave. In the elevator, I replay //you don't get to ask that yet// and realize the important word isn't "ask." It's "yet." She's going to tell me. Someday. When she decides I'm ready for it.

Which means she has an answer. Which means there is a plan. Which means the panties are step one.

I'm in the car before I realize I didn't ask what step two is. I'm on the highway before I realize I didn't need to. I already know it involves a bra.

