:: R4_Choice_C [r4 story]
<<location "Victoria Cross's Office, Floor 42">>
<<objective "Leave Victoria's office.">>

I say nothing.

The silence sits between us like an object. Solid. Present. Victoria lets it exist. She doesn't fill it. She doesn't prompt. She picks up her pen and looks down at her paper and writes and the sound of the nib on the page is the only sound in the room.

I should speak. Ask a question. Make a demand. Reassert some version of the man who walked into this building twelve hours ago with polished shoes and a firm handshake. That man would have said something. That man would have negotiated.

That man didn't wear silk panties to work and get hard in a conference room.

The silence stretches. Ten seconds. Twenty. Long enough that it stops being awkward and starts being something else. A statement. A position. A surrender that doesn't need words because the words would only get in the way of what my silence already says.

Victoria looks up. Studies me. Something shifts in her eyes. Not warmth exactly. Recognition. The look of a woman who just watched someone pass a test they didn't know they were taking.

<<say "Victoria Cross">>Good. You're learning.<</say>>

She sets the pen down. Folds her hands.

I leave her office. In the elevator, I think about what I'm learning. I'm not sure I could name it. But I know the lesson involves silence, and panties, and the discovery that sometimes the strongest thing a man can do is close his mouth and feel the lace against his skin and let the woman in the corner office decide what happens next.

